  "text_pages": [
    "International Dormitory | Student Life | Chiba University of Commerce\nHome\n>\nStudent Life\n>\nInternational Dormitory\nInternational Dormitory\nLocation\n1-3-1 Konodai, Ichikawa-shi, Chiba 272-8512 Japan\n1-minute walk from the main gate of the University.\nQualifications\nExchange students from CUC partner universities\nInternational students of CUC\nCheck the application guideline announced by CUC for the application process.\nBoarding fee\nBoarding fee per month (yen)\n¥38,000 per month\nBoarding fee includes utilities (gas, water, electricity) and internet communication.\nFloor plan\nThe unit consists of two or three (in the case of a triple room) private rooms for individual use and a shared kitchen, dining room, bathroom, toilet, and balcony. As a general rule, two people will live in one unit.\nFacilities\nPrivate room\nDesk and chair\nAir conditioner\nDesk light\nBed frame (no mattress or other bedding is provided)\nShared facility\nKitchen\nIH cooktop\nMicrowave oven\nRefrigerator\nDining table and chairs\nTableware and utensils\nWashing machine\nBathroom sink\nToilet\nBathroom\nBalcony\nRemarks\nThe rooms are not equipped with supplies (towels, detergent, hair-dryer, etc.).\nMeals\nThe International Dormitory has no cafeteria and no meal plan, so please prepare your own meals or use the cafeterias on campus.\nInternational Cultural Exchange Room\nThe International Cultural Exchange Room can be used for exchange and event purposes. The room is available for use by international students, including exchange students in the International Dormitory, and CUC students who support international students.\nHours of use: 10:00-23:00 daily (except during long vacations)\nReturn to Top"
  ],
